O|                         
O|                         
S|          EXT. CAMP - LATER
O|                         
N|          Fitzgerald sleeping off that whiskey. The others snoring in
N|          a cluster at the center of the camp. Henry lies there
N|          awake... looks across to Glass, still sitting against the
N|          tree, a HANDRAWN MAP in his lap, as his eyes pierce the
N|          darkness. Henry eases over to Glass.
O|                         
C|                          HENRY
U|           Can't sleep either?
O|                         
C|                          GLASS
U|           Never like closin' my eyes when I'm
U|           not sure who'll be standin' over me
U|           when I open `em.
O|                         
C|                          HENRY
U|           I keep thinking about Boone and the
U|           others... how maybe I should've had
U|           us make camp further up river.
O|                         
C|                          GLASS
U|           The tracks I saw... those `Ree had
U|           been tailin' us for a while. They'd
U|           have gone as far north as it took.
P|                          (BEAT)
U|           You're a good man, Captain. Soon
U|           as you realize that, these others
U|           will too.
O|                         
N|          Henry likes hearing that... still isn't sure it's true.
O|           13.
O|                         
C|                          HENRY
U|           Your years trappin' and guidin' out
U|           here... have you had much
