N|          BACK ROOM. The O.S. SHUFFLING OF FEET.
O|                         
N|          Glass freezes... he isn't alone. He rises... grabs a
N|          splintered post like a spear... eases toward the doorway...
N|          raises the post to swing...
O|           51.
O|                         
N|          ...and sees the SMALL PUPPY standing in the back room. The
N|          dog takes off around a crumbled wall. Glass follows it.
O|                         
O|                         
S|          INT. LODGE/BACK ROOM - CONTINUOUS
O|                         
N|          Glass limps across the room... turns the corner of the
N|          crumbled wall... and sees the dog slide to a stop beside an
N|          ANCIENT ARIKARA SQUAW, huddled in the corner, her bony arms
N|          outstretched in front of her in weak defense. And her eyes
N|          are SOLID WHITE... the old woman is blind. She CRIES OUT A
N|          CHANT over and over... her death chant, as she waits for this
N|          stranger to kill her.
O|                         
N|          Glass stands frozen... confused. He tries to speak, but his
N|          throat still won't let him. He crouches down in front of the
N|          old woman... reaches for her hand, but she flails him away.
N|          He grabs her again... gently... just holds it until she
N|          calms... studying the woman... her hollow face all skin and
N|          bones... she's obviously dying.
O|                         
N|          He pulls the strip of buffalo meat from his pocket... pushes
N|          it into the squaw's hand. She immediately jerks it to her
N|          mouth... and that's when Glass sees the WOMAN HAS NO TEETH...
N|          she can't eat.
O|                         
N|          Glass turns to an old pot tipped over on the floor.
O|                         
O|                         
S|          EXT. BURNED ARIKARA VILLAGE - DAY
O|                         
N|          Glass carries the pot toward a nearby stream. The dog
N|          scurries out behind him... follows Glass to the water.
O|                         
O|                         
S|          INT. LODGE/BACK ROOM - DAY
O|                         
N|          The pot boils over burning logs. Glass dips a cup in,
N|          pulling out a warm broth. He carries it to the squaw, still
N|          sitting in the corner... takes her hand, placing the cup in
N|          it for her. She gulps the liquid back.
O|                         
N|          Glass goes back to refill the cup. The old woman MUMBLES
N|          SOMETHING we can't understand... over and over, as Glass
N|          brings the cup back to her. He tries to ease it into her
N|          hand, but the woman pushes it away... slides her hand up
N|          Glass' arm to his face... patting it... MUMBLING THOSE SAME
N|          WORDS... thanking Glass.
O|           52.
O|                         
O|                         
