O|                         
N|          Glass has stacked several burned posts into a crude pyre at
N|          the edge of the village. The squaw lies atop the pyre,
N|          covered in the blankets he gathered for her. Glass stands
N|          beside the pyre, a FLAMING TORCH in his hand. The puppy
N|          rests at his feet.
O|                         
O|                         
