U|           Three days on horse?
O|                         
N|          Spotted Horse nods... looks Glass over, and shakes his head.
O|                         
C|                          SPOTTED HORSE
U|           Not walk. Hides soon.
O|                         
N|          Glass doesn't understand... until Spotted Horse points to a
N|          ROW OF BUFFALO HIDES hanging from a line.
O|                         
C,E|           Spotted Horse (cont'd)
U|           We trade Bra-zo.
O|                         
N|          Glass stares at the tanning hides, then down at his leg.
N|          Finally, he nods. Spotted Horse starts walking... waves for
N|          Glass to follow.
O|                         
C,E|           Spotted Horse (cont'd)
U|           Come. Eat.
O|                         
N|          Glass follows after him. The children sneak in behind,
N|          giggling as they tail Glass across camp.
O|                         
N|          Glass glances back... New Moon and Little One duck behind a
N|          tee-pee... wait for him to continue before they scoot back
N|          out after him.
O|           64.
O|                         
O|                         
S|          INT. CHIEF'S LODGE - NIGHT
O|                         
N|          Glass, Spotted Horse, Three Feathers, Running Fox and OTHER
N,I|          WARRIORS sit around a fire, eating with CHIEF RED HAWK, the
N|          Medicine Man, and several other TRIBAL ELDERS.
O|                         
C|                          GLASS
U|           The men stole my rifle.
O|                         
N|          The Sioux don't understand. Glass reaches over, taking
N|          Spotted Horse's plate.
O|                         
C,E|                          GLASS (CONT'D)
U|           They took. They took...
O|                         
N|          Glass aims an imaginary rifle.
O|                         
C,E|                          GLASS (CONT'D)
U|           ...my rifle. My gear.
O|                         
N|          Now Spotted Horse understands... translates for the others.
O|                         
C,E|                          GLASS (CONT'D)
U|           They left me to die. So I mean to
U|           find `em both. Get my rifle back.
O|                         
N|          Spotted Horse translates again. Red Hawk nods, studying
N|          Glass.
O|                         
N|          Red Hawk SAYS SOMETHING to Glass... motions to the BEAR CLAW
N|          NECKLACE. Glass looks to Spotted Horse.
O|                         
C|                          SPOTTED HORSE
U|           Red Hawk ask who kill griz-lee.
O|                         
N|          Glass touches his chest. Red Hawk nods, impressed. Glass
N|          points to the JAGGED SCARS running up Red Hawk's neck to a
N|          MISSING RIGHT EAR.
O|                         
C|                          GLASS
U|           Grizzly?
O|                         
N|          Red Hawk smiles... shakes his head.
O|                         
C|                          RED HAWK
U|           Arikara.
O|                         
N|          That word, Glass understands. Red Hawk rambles a long
N|          sentence in Sioux. The other members LAUGH.
O|           65.
O|                         
C|                          SPOTTED HORSE
U|           He say Arikara take right ear of
U|           Sioux. Left ear of whites. Not
U|           know what they take from you.
O|                         
N|          Glass smiles along with the others. They continue their meal.
O|                         
O|                         
S|          EXT. SIOUX VILLAGE - DAY
O|                         
N|          Snow falls over Glass, as he stands outside the tee-pee,
N|          flexing his injured leg... putting more weight on it...
N|          testing its recovered strength.
O|                         
N|          Suddenly, a SPEAR PLANTS INTO THE GROUND BETWEEN HIS FEET.
N|          Glass turns, startled... sees Spotted Horse, Three Feathers,
N|          Running Fox, and several OTHER WARRIORS staring at him.
O|                         
N|          Glass' eyes jump from the spear to the warriors, unsure.
O|                         
N|          Spotted Horse strides to Glass... grabs the spear, then spins
N|          it sideways... stares at Glass, until a smile spreads across
N|          Spotted Horse's face... he holds the spear out to Glass.
O|                         
C|                          SPOTTED HORSE
U|           Buff-A-lo Man hunt with Sioux?
O|                         
N|          Glass relaxes... nods... takes the spear from Spotted Horse.
N|          Three Feathers hands a BUFFALO HIDE to Glass... motions for
N|          Glass to put it on.
O|                         
C|                          THREE FEATHERS
U|           Tatanka Wicasa.
O|                         
N|          Glass wraps the hide around him. The Warriors smile and nod.
O|                         
O|                         
S|          EXT. FOREST - DAY
O|                         
N,G|          A world of silent white... like we're inside a giant snow-
N,G|          globe. The sky is emptying all the snow it has over us...
N|          pouring down... the only sound comes from the flakes hitting
N|          the already fallen snow. The pale trunks of Cottonwoods rise
N|          up from the white ground.
O|                         
N|          Then out of the white... a SHAPE APPEARS... a GIANT WOLF
N|          WALKING ON ITS HIND LEGS. But as the wolf comes closer, we
N,G|          see it's not a wolf at all... it's THREE FEATHERS, wearing
N|          his WOLF SKIN. He CRIES OUT... HOWLING WILDLY.
O|                         
N|          A few yards beside him, another WARRIOR is doing the same...
N|          CHANTING... beating his spear against the Cottonwoods as he
N|          walks.
O|           66.
O|                         
O|                         
N|          GLASS - WEARING THE BUFFALO HIDE...
O|                         
N|          ...walking slowly through the trees, carrying the spear.
N|          Yellow Bear is beside him... motions for Glass to spread out.
O|                         
O|                         
N,G|          FROM ABOVE THE TREES...
O|                         
N,G|          ...we see the fur-covered warriors are formed into a wide
N|          circle... and slowly converging... YELLING... pounding their
N|          spears... making as much noise as possible, as they tighten
N|          their ring.
O|                         
O|                         
N,G|          POV FROM THE BRUSH...
O|                         
N|          ...watching DISTANT CHANTING WARRIORS pushing through the
N,G|          trees. V.O. SNORTING... our POV darts sideways... charges
N,G|          through the brush... slides to a stop when we see Running Fox
N,G|          moving toward us... spins back another direction.
O|                         
O|                         
N|          GLASS - MOVING THROUGH THE FOREST...
O|                         
N|          ...the falling snow clinging to his face... covering the
N|          buffalo hide.
O|                         
N|          And then a MASSIVE SHAPE BLASTS through the trees ahead of
N|          him. Glass freezes, his grip tightening on the spear. He
N|          looks to Spotted Horse, who nods... YELLS OUT, beating his
N|          spear against the trees, and motioning for Glass to do the
N|          same.
O|                         
N|          Glass is apprehensive at first... just lightly tapping his
N|          spear. But as the other warriors' chants grow, Glass gets
N|          caught up in the hunt... begins beating the trees... YELLING
N|          as loud as his throat will allow.
O|                         
O|                         
N|          THE WARRIORS - EYES PIERCING THROUGH THE SNOW... CHANTING...
N|          BEATING THE BUSHES.
O|                         
O|                         
N,G|          OUR LOW POV AGAIN - RACING CHAOTICALLY THROUGH THE BRUSH...
O|                         
N|          ...to Spotted Horse waving his spear... back over the snow...
N,G|          to Three Feathers SCREAMING... we spin again... crash through
N,G|          bushes, then suddenly TUMBLE... DROP THROUGH THE SNOW.
O|           67.
O|                         
O|                         
N|          GLASS - HEARING THE ANIMAL'S WAIL...
O|                         
N|          ...seeing Spotted Horse pick up his pace... start trotting
N|          forward. Glass does the same... all the hunters converging
N|          around a LARGE BLACK HOLE IN THE SNOW...
O|                         
N|          ...and the ELK trapped at the bottom.
O|                         
N|          The warriors cry out victoriously... begin DRIVING THEIR
N|          SPEARS INTO THE TRAP, killing the animal.
O|                         
O|                         
S|          EXT. SIOUX VILLAGE - EVENING
O|                         
N|          The elk roasts over a fire at the center of the village.
N|          Glass sits alone outside the tee-pee, using the sharp tip of
N|          the spear to carve into a small chunk of wood.
O|                         
N|          As he carves, New Moon and Little One sneak around the tee-
N|          pee behind him... watch Glass work. Glass hears them
N|          GIGGLING... doesn't react... just keeps carving... tilts the
N|          long handle of the spear as he works, tapping the side of the
N|          tee-pee, and SHAKING LOOSE A CLUMP OF SNOW DOWN ONTO THE
N|          BOYS.
O|                         
N|          The shocked boys freeze in the cold... wipe the snow from
N|          their faces to see Glass grinning at them. The little boys
N|          charge Glass, leaping onto him... wrestling him to the
N|          ground, as they squeeze his hair.
O|                         
C|                          BOYS
U|           Tatanka Wicasa! Tatanka Wicasa!
O|                         
N|          Spotted Horse stands across the village, watching Glass and
N|          the boys play in the snow.
O|                         
O|                         
S|          EXT. SIOUX VILLAGE - NIGHT
O|                         
N|          Glass stands at the edge of the village, carving at the wood
N|          with the spear tip, and watching the Sioux from a distance.
N|          Yellow Bear sees him... approaches, carrying his SON on his
N|          shoulders. The little boy gnaws on a strip of meat.
O|                         
N|          Spotted Horse holds out a bowl of food to Glass.
O|                         
C|                          GLASS
U|           Thank you.
O|                         
C|                          SPOTTED HORSE
U|           Good hunt.
O|           68.
O|                         
C|                          GLASS
U|           Yes.
O|                         
N|          Glass smiles up at Spotted Horse's son.
O|                         
C|                          SPOTTED HORSE
U|           You. Fam-i-lee?
O|                         
C|                          GLASS
P|           (shakes his head)
U|           No.
O|                         
C|                          SPOTTED HORSE
U|           No wom-an?
P|           (pointing to son)
U|           Wakayaja?
O|                         
N|          A long beat, then...
O|                         
C|                          GLASS
U|           No. Not for a long time.
O|                         
N|          Glass continues eating... watches Spotted Horse bounce the
N|          giggling little boy on his shoulders.
O|                         
O|                         
S|          EXT. SIOUX VILLAGE - DAY
O|                         
