N|          village.
O|                         
O|                         
S|          EXT. WILDERNESS - DAY
O|                         
N|          Glass, Spotted Horse and Three Feathers ride along a high
N|          ridge, surrounded by empty snow-covered wilderness. They
N|          have the world to themselves.
O|                         
O|                         
S|          EXT. CAMP - NIGHT
O|                         
N|          Glass crouches over a shallow, five-foot long hole surrounded
N|          by deep snow. The hole is filled with small fires and rocks.
N|          And he's watching Spotted Horse and Three Feathers tossing
N|          rocks into their own matching holes, then dragging the dirt
N|          back into them. Spotted Horse throws a glance back to Glass,
N|          making sure he understands.
O|                         
N|          Glass nods... pulls the dirt back in, covering the flames.
N|          He watches Spotted Horse spread a blanket over the warm
N|          ground, then does the same. He sits on the mound of dirt...
N|          leans back against a tree... feels the warmth rise up from
N|          beneath him.
O|                         
N|          He nods to Spotted Horse, who is already resting under his
N|          blanket.
O|                         
C|                          GLASS
U|           Nice.
O|                         
C|                          SPOTTED HORSE
P|                          (NODS)
U|           Nice.
O|                         
N|          Glass pulls the buffalo hide around himself... keeping watch.
O|                         
C,E|           SPOTTED HORSE (cont'd)
U|           Sleep. No Arikara.
O|                         
N|          Glass nods... but still doesn't close his eyes. Spotted
N|          Horse tosses his knife over beside Glass. Glass takes it...
N|          nods to Spotted Horse.
O|                         
C,E|           SPOTTED HORSE (cont'd)
U|           Me sleep.
O|           70.
O|                         
N|          Spotted Horse rolls over, turning his back on Glass...
N|          trusting him with the knife. Three Feathers does the same.
O|                         
N|          Glass just stares out into the night.
O|                         
O|                         
S|          INT. FORT UNION/BUNKHOUSE - NIGHT
O|                         
N|          Dark and quiet... except for the SNORING of a few men.
N|          Fitzgerald sleeps on his cot. A shadow glides across him...
N|          hovers over his face.
O|                         
N|          Fitzgerald's eyes blink open.
