S|          EXT. FORT BRAZEAU - DAY
O|                         
N|          Just a small cluster of log buildings sitting along the banks
N|          of the Missouri. Dozens of tee-pees and tents are set up
N|          outside the complex.
O|                         
N|          Glass follows Spotted Horse and Three Feathers into the camp.
N|          BEGGING INDIANS and DRUNK TRAPPERS paw at the men as they
N|          ride past, pleading for handouts.
O|           71.
O|                         
N|          One of the Indians grabs for the hides. Three Feathers
N|          plants his foot in the Indian's chest... shoves him back into
N|          the snow.
O|                         
N|          They continue on... climb off their horses outside the
N|          TRADING POST. Three Feathers stays to guard the hides, as
N|          Spotted Horse and Glass enter.
O|                         
O|                         
S|          INT. TRADING POST - DAY
O|                         
N|          A small, dingy room lined with shelves, all stacked high with
N|          pots, pans, dry goods, whiskey, blankets, weapons... anything
N,I|          that can be traded. KIOWA BRAZEAU, (60's), French-Canadian,
N|          stands behind the counter... looks up when the BELL over the
N|          door RINGS... sees Spotted Horse with Glass behind.
O|                         
C|                          BRAZEAU
P|           (thick French accent)
U|           Bon jour, Spotted Horse. You come
U|           with many hides I hope.
P|           (off Spotted Horse's nod)
U|           We make good trades then.
O|                         
N|          Brazeau's eyes lock on Glass... stares at him, unsure.
O|                         
C,E|                          BRAZEAU (CONT'D)
U|           Monsieur Glass?
O|                         
C|                          GLASS
U|           Good to see you again, Mr. Brazeau.
O|                         
C|                          BRAZEAU
U|           Jesus Christ, what happened to your
U|           goddamned face?
O|                         
C|                          GLASS
U|           Had a tussle with a grizzly.
O|                         
N|          Glass shakes Brazeau's hand. Brazeau studies his face...
N|          notices the Bear Claw Necklace... smiles.
O|                         
C|                          BRAZEAU
U|           And now the grizzly, he don't look
U|           so good either, eh?
O|                         
N|          Glass shakes his head.
O|                         
C,E|                          BRAZEAU (CONT'D)
P|           (off Spotted Horse)
U|           You run with the Sioux these days?
O|           72.
O|                         
C|                          GLASS
U|           They looked after me for a spell.
U|           I'm on my way to catch back up with
U|           Captain Henry... at Fort Union.
U|           Needed to trade for some supplies
U|           on the Company's credit if I could.
O|                         
C|                          BRAZEAU
U|           Oui, of course. Anything you like.
O|                         
